think Checked for an existing loom before building one, which is the waste this fleet keeps naming. tools/g/glow_rune_alphabet_worker.sh already holds the derived population against the pronunciation roll, three G1 briefs and the TAME family index. So the repair is a fourth binding inside that worker rather than a second census.
think The three elder bindings each ask for a NAME, which is why all three passed while a rune stood untaught. |+ barlus was named 20260822, carries STOA332-336, is parsed at rune_shop_gate.rye:parse_body and folded by seven src/gate/ sources, and no page of the Glow Book named it.
think ?& and ?| take the same named exemption they already hold one binding over: an entry leads with its spoken name, so a glyph the closed table cannot pronounce is a glyph the reference cannot head an entry with. One custody question, two pages, Keaton's word.
obs The control's pen is a worktree at HEAD and copied exactly one working-tree file, the worker. The widened worker met HEAD's reference page and 18 checks failed for a fault the working tree had already repaired -- half-current is worse than either whole. All eight files the worker binds are copied in now.
obs Two whole-wall mutations bitten: the book exemption loop removed entire (pass 30 fail 2), and the page-presence check removed (pass 31 fail 1). The second cost only one check because the exemption wall then catches the same plant under the wrong name -- honest, and named here rather than smoothed over.
obs The REDS row cannot land. The pin reads 40,831 of 40,960 with rows_that_fit=0, pin_foldable_rows=1, and pin_upstream_differs -- so a fold is lawful only after a rebase and costs a shelf head for a peer's row. The finding's key is its stamp, 20260911.202958, per the derived-spine law.
